        "original_id": "7613e546-257c-5f88-858d-eee8c6bb9471",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Street Survivors\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd\n- People: Steve Gaines, Ronnie Van Zant, Allen Collins, Cassie Gaines\n- Topics: Southern rock\n\nFacts:\n- Street Survivors is the fifth studio album by Southern rock band Lynyrd Skynyrd, and it was released on October 17, 1977.\n- Street Survivors is the last Lynyrd Skynyrd album recorded by original members Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- Street Survivors is the only Lynyrd Skynyrd studio recording featuring guitarist Steve Gaines.\n- Steve Gaines was born on September 14, 1949, and he was an American musician.\n- Steve Gaines was a guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for Lynyrd Skynyrd from May 11, 1976 until his death on October 20, 1977.\n- Steve Gaines was the younger brother of Cassie Gaines, who was a backup vocalist for Lynyrd Skynyrd's live performances.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
